        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a7e6cb79-00d1-587f-9365-497d71f25c65",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Cold Harbor, Second Battle of Bull Run\n- People: David P. Casey\n- Places: Virginia, Prince William County\n- Awards: Medal of Honor\n\nFacts:\n- The Second Battle of Bull Run, also called the Battle of Second Manassas, was fought on August 28–30, 1862, in Prince William County, Virginia, as part of the American Civil War.\n- The Battle of Cold Harbor was fought from May 31 to June 12, 1864, and its most significant fighting occurred on June 3.\n- David P. Casey received the Medal of Honor, the highest United States award for bravery in combat, for his actions at the Battle of Cold Harbor in Virginia on June 3, 1864.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1c522b46-e91e-5f98-ae42-e348f6638b12",
        "text": "Page: Battle of Cold Harbor. Sentence: The Battle of Cold Harbor was fought from May 31 to June 12, 1864, with the most significant fighting occurring on June 3.\nPage: Second Battle of Bull Run. Sentence: The Second Battle of Bull Run or Battle of Second Manassas was fought August 28–30, 1862 in Prince William County, Virginia, as part of the American Civil War.\nPage: David P. Casey. Sentence: Casey received the United States' highest award for bravery during combat, the Medal of Honor, for his action during the Battle of Cold Harbor in Virginia on 3 June 1864.",
